+Recurrently adequate theories may nevertheless be absent from $A_i^{*}$ because they were rejected before $G_2$ or are stochastically false-rejected afterward.
 If $A_i^{*}\neq\emptysetset$, agent $i$ is eventually never dissonant.
 If $A_i^{*}=\emptysetset$, it is eventually always dissonant; since no election occurs after $G^{*}$, the mechanical rule gives $\lambda_i^{(k_i)}\widehat B_i<\gamma_i$ at every such period, so agent $i$ is in dissonant stasis (\cref{def:stasis})---including the zero-leverage, abandoned-question, and irreparable cases.
 Taking the union over the countably many $(G_2,\sigma^{*})$ gives the claim on all of $E$.
